    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 136\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 1099, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  education law, in relation to enacting the\n      \"freedom to read act\"\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill requires the state education department and  school  library\nsystems  to  adopt  policies according to which school library staff are\nempowered to curate the  widest  array  of  developmentally  appropriate\nlibrary materials.\n \n  I  recognize the important role school library staff play in promoting\nstudent learning and the democratic values of free inquiry and tolerance\nfor diversity of thought. School librarians  already  maintain  academic\nfreedom  over  pedagogical decisions to the same extent as teachers, and\nschools are already prohibited from  restricting  access  to  texts  and\nmaterials  simply  because  school  officials  disagree or disapprove of\ntheir content. Additionally, the state education department  has  previ-\nously  issued guidance on library curation and quality collection devel-\nopment designed to ensure that a broad range of perspectives and experi-\nences are represented in school learning materials. I am concerned  that\nthe unclear wording of this bill will do more to confuse than to clarify\nschools' obligations and school librarians' roles.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
